        "created_at": "2015-04-29T23:52:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Silverleaf\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/48/2332_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Silverleaf:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><strong>Azqa wrote:</strong><br><blockquote>Oh, I'll add Citadels to the list. &nbsp;2-8 players, not much to set up but has a lot of replayability. &nbsp;Another citybuilding theme, with semi-drafting mechanics for roles on a round-by-round basis. &nbsp;Tends to play pretty quickly.</blockquote></div>\nI can't read this without hearing Eric Summerer in my head shouting \"CITADELLLLLLLLLLLS!\"\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I've been known to yell this aloud when Citadels is mentioned. No one ever gets it.</p>",
