        "created_at": "2015-04-30T02:54:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Craig\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/craig/48/2150_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Craig:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Silverleaf wrote:</b><br><blockquote><strong>Azqa wrote:</strong><br><blockquote>Oh, I'll add Citadels to the list. &nbsp;2-8 players, not much to set up but has a lot of replayability. &nbsp;Another citybuilding theme, with semi-drafting mechanics for roles on a round-by-round basis. &nbsp;Tends to play pretty quickly.</blockquote>\nI can't read this without hearing Eric Summerer in my head shouting \"CITADELLLLLLLLLLLS!\"\n</blockquote></div>\nI've been known to yell this aloud when Citadels is mentioned. No one ever gets it. \n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Welcome to my world then… I'm constantly doing memes and in-jokes at the wrong target group, so I get a lot of blank looks.</p>\n<p>I'd totally get your Eric reference. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
